I think you can use `UCharCast`, which is safer than the c-style pointer cast? Is this change needed? sorry, no! gonna change it Done Seems like those are unneeded too. cc @dergoegge  I think we should still call `bitcoinconsensus_verify_script_with_spent_outputs` when `n_in` is too large. Just only allocate when it's not.

(I initially pointed this out in https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/28539#issuecomment-1741775909 but my email client messed up my message, sorry about that.) Done, thanks!  In 35bcc70c1b44921d7da0207ba4d70a2c114e8ba1 "lib: add Taproot support to libconsensus"

nit: Seems like this check could be pushed into `verify_script` to avoid having to duplicate it across all of the `verify_script_*` variations. Thanks, if I touch the code again, I address it. Same as for the other two pointer parameters (`scriptPubKey` and `txTo`), I think `spentOutputs` should also follow const-correctness for consistency and type-safety reasons (otherwise this suggests to the caller that the passed `UTXO` instance could be modified inside):
```suggestion
                                    const UTXO *spentOutputs, unsigned int spentOutputsLen,
```
 more of a nit, but could compare with the input parameter `spentOutputsLen` instead and do the error checking before the for loop (as early as possible) Makes sense, I'm gonna address it. done done ```suggestion
typedef struct {
    const unsigned char *scriptPubKey;
    unsigned int scriptPubKeySize;
    int64_t value;
} UTXO;
```
as the current API header leads to an error if compiled with C:

