this needs to be a `std::abort()` (or similar), otherwise out of process fuzzers like afl will not catch this as a crash (by default at least) You may be able to confirm this with `AFL_CRASH_EXITCODE='1'` (i.e. tell afl++ to treat exit(1) as a crash) thx, fixed! Should this also be an `abort()`, or should the commit message be adjusted to say something else than "Abort"? nit: Try to adhere to symbol naming convention from *developer-notes.md*?
```suggestion
extern std::atomic<bool> g_seeded_prng_zero;
extern std::atomic<bool> g_used_prng;
``` nit: Naming + `static`
```suggestion
static bool g_ever_used_prng{false};
``` Bug in that it can be reset if called with `FIXED_SEED` afterwards:
```suggestion
    seeded_g_prng_zero |= seedtype == SeedRand::ZEROS;
```

