Yeah absolutely. Good eye. If you compare it in-detail, that function is a plain copy of `AbortNode`: it (1) calls `SetMiscWarning`, (2) logs the error, (3) notifies the UI by calling `InitError` (noui listeners as well) and (4) calls to the shutdown function..
So, we can just get rid of it. Code review ACK d44dd73bcabc694880dfc966fad21980cd3b4c64. But it would be nice to extend this change to work with bitcoin-qt as well. I also think it would be good to apply the following changes, which replace the `bool shutdown_due_error` global with an `int exit_status{EXIT_SUCCESS}` `NodeContext` member. 

