The bug was introduced by _not_ updating this line in #28246 to use the `CTxDestination` returned by `DecodeDestination` directly in the `CRecipient` object. Instead, it was converting to a `CScript` and silently converting to a `CNoDestination`, since `CRecipient` now expects a `CTxDestination`. So if we had marked the `CNoDestination` constructor as explicit, the compiler would have warned us here.

I changed it back to try and use the `CScript` directly in the `CRecipient` and confirmed I got a compiler warning:

